Phone chat UI (#115, ADR-0013), after ChatGPT's conventions. The user's message is a bubble on the end side (left in
RTL, right in LTR: brand.css mirrors upstream's physical margin) with a hook class for its EF colour; on touch screens
its actions appear when the bubble is tapped instead of under every message. The chat header gets a hook for its solid
bar; the phone drawer leaves a strip of the chat to tap (upstream's own option, now on by default); the system bar is
white like the top bar (theme colour and the iOS status bar). Accessibility: a code block's scroll area takes keyboard
focus, because it scrolls sideways on phones, and the collapsed desktop side panel is inert like the phone drawer.
index.html links the direction-aware reply styles (brand assets/ef-chat.css, served as is: PostCSS compiles logical
properties to LTR and :dir() to an ancestor [dir] test).

